      <section class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 mb-16 items-center">
         <div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-blue-900 mb-6">The District 02 IEP Environment</h2>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4">
               [cite_start]District 02 is known as Manhattan's highest-wealth district, characterized by a massive high school commuter population and a highly engaged parent body. [cite: 1] However, this environment creates unique pressures within the Committee on Special Education (CSE).
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6">
               [cite_start]Families here frequently report that high-stakes neuropsychological evaluations and the pursuit of private placement (often through "Carter Cases") dominate the local CSE culture. [cite: 1] Managing <a href="/iep/states/new-york/new-york-timeline/" class="text-blue-600 underline font-medium">the New York IEP timeline</a> is critical here, as implementation disputes often escalate into high-legal-risk scenarios.
            </p>
            <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-pink-500 bg-pink-50 p-6 rounded-r-lg italic text-gray-700 mb-6">
               "In District 2, the conversation moves very quickly from 'how can the school help' to 'which private school will we need a settlement for.' The pressure on the CSE to provide high-level services is intense."
            </blockquote>
         </div>
         <div class="bg-blue-50 p-8 rounded-2xl border border-blue-100">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-900 mb-4">Quick District Stats</h3>
